WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.883
In tutorial 7.1, you'll
read your website overview,

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.322
and see how your site
is doing at a glance.

00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:18.343
First, open Overview. The top row
shows your clicks, your impressions,

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:22.878
the times you showed up in search, your
average position and visits from search,

00:00:22.928 --> 00:00:24.664
against the four weeks before.

00:00:25.678 --> 00:00:28.918
On the right, Next step names
the one thing to do first,

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.624
with a button that opens it.

00:00:32.107 --> 00:00:35.407
Below, Coming up shows what
your next weekly run will do.

00:00:35.457 --> 00:00:40.668
Then four cards show your site's health,
AI answers, links and top 10 keywords.

00:00:42.178 --> 00:00:46.253
Next, Top recommendations lists
the most urgent steps first.

00:00:46.303 --> 00:00:50.199
Click Why it matters to see the
reason, then use the button beside it.

00:00:51.628 --> 00:00:54.328
Then Search performance
shows a year of clicks.

00:00:54.378 --> 00:00:58.778
Switch to Impressions or Position.
The numbered marks show new pages,

00:00:58.828 --> 00:01:00.573
audits and search updates.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:05.965
Beside it, Ranking movers shows which
keywords moved since last week's check.

00:01:08.174 --> 00:01:12.379
Further down, follow your health,
AI answers and links over time,

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:16.655
then check your content pipeline,
open alerts and the latest reports.

00:01:18.107 --> 00:01:20.932
Every card and panel opens its own page,

00:01:20.982 --> 00:01:24.833
so Overview is the place to start
each week, and see what changed.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:30.177
So, read the headline numbers, check
the cards and the recommendations,

00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:33.322
look at search performance,
and follow the trends below.

00:01:34.331 --> 00:01:40.030
Now you can read your overview. Next, read
your search and traffic in tutorial 7.2.
